      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Is that a PC player? I've only see Quest users have that problem. Neato\n\nI think you might be better served by moving your world, any issue with syncing a player load in, including problems they haven't written yet will cause an avatar to display there. They can obviously fix the ones they know about, but not really the ones they haven't caused yet, so the problem wont exactly stay fixed in a long term. Heck at one point I had an avatar with a world drop that dropped at the origin point.",
